load @term/seed/group/coxeter
  find coxeter-group

load @term/seed/structure/set
  find set

# A Weyl group: the finite reflection group of a root system, the symmetries of the roots of a Lie algebra. It is the
# Coxeter group generated by the reflections in the hyperplanes perpendicular to the roots. The Weyl group of F4, the
# full symmetry group of the 24-cell, has order one thousand one hundred fifty-two, and its threefold diagram symmetry
# is triality, the interchange of the vector and the two spinor representations that is unique to dimension eight. The
# form carries the underlying Coxeter group and the root system; the order and symmetry counts are machine-checked in
# the F4 file.
form weyl-group
  link reflections, like coxeter-group
  link roots, like set
